    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Vedalken Classes (Customizable Origins)",
      "sourceAnchor": "classes-custom-origin",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-classes-custom-origin-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "This section assumes that you’re using the option “"
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Customizing Your Origin",
              "href": "https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/tcoe/character-options#CustomizingYourOrigin"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "” rules presented in Tasha’s Cauldron of Everything. If you’re not using those rules, scroll down to the next section."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-artificer",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Artificer",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-artificer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-artificer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Between doubling your proficiency bonus with tools and Tireless Precision, no one can compete with the Artificer’s capabilities with tools. Vedalken Dispassion provides a helpful defense which nicely complements the Artificer’s typically very high AC, and protects you from things that can’t be handled by things like Absorb Elements or infusions."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-barbarian",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Barbarian",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-barbarian",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-barbarian-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A skill and a tool give the Barbarian something useful to do outside of\n\tcombat, and Vedalken Dispassion protects you from effects which can usually\n\tincapacitate martial characters with ease."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-bard",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Bard",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-bard",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-bard-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Fun fact: musical instruments are classified as a tool. That’s right! You can\n\tget a 1d4 bonus with your favorite instrument! You also get an extra skill,\n\twhich could absolutely be Performance in order to get a d4 added to that, too.\n\tThen, with the rules in Xanathar’s you can combine your proficiency in an\n\tinstrument with a Performance check and potentially add both d4’s and roll at\n\tAdvantage, potentially with Expertise depending on which Expertise options you\n\ttake at level 3."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-bard-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Beyond that fun interaction, Tireless Precision can also add a d4 to one of\n\tyour favorite skills, stacking with Expertise to make you profoundly good at\n\twhichever skill you choose."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-cleric",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Cleric",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-cleric",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-cleric-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Clerics don’t have much use for tools, and their saving throws are mostly\n\talready good since they’re proficienct in both Wisdom and Charisma saves."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-druid",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Druid",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-druid",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-druid-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Druids don’t have much use for tools, and their saving throws are already good since they’re proficient in both Intelligence and Wisdom saves."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-fighter",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Fighter",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-fighter",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-fighter-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A skill and a tool give the Fighter something useful to do outside of combat,\n\tand Vedalken Dispassion protects you from effects which can usually\n\tincapacitate martial characters with ease."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-monk",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Monk",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-monk",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-monk-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "An extra skill helps close the skill gap between the Monk and the Rogue,\n\tespecially with the extra d4 to somewhat make up for Expertise. Monks are\n\tproficienct in Strength and Dexterity saves until you get Diamond Body at\n\tlevel 14, so Vedalken Dispassion provides an extremely useful defense until\n\tyou hit that point."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-paladin",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Paladin",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-paladin",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-paladin-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "An extra skill and a tool will help you expand beyond Face skills. Vedalken\n\tDispassion provides some protection on mental saves until Aura of Protection\n\tcomes online. Because this build is so incredibly defensive, I recommend\n\tputting your ability score increases into either Strength or Dexterity and\n\tConstitution and focus primarily on offense, otherwise you’re fall into tank\n\tfalacy territory."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-ranger",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Ranger",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-ranger",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-ranger-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Ranger’s Wisdom saving throws aren’t so bad as the Barbarian or the\n\tFighters, but they’re not proficienct in any mental saves, so Vedalken\n\tDispassion is a great defense. Tireless Precision helps close the skipp gap\n\tbetween the ranger and the rogue."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-rogue",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Rogue",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-rogue",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-rogue-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Using Tireless Precision on your favorite skill (I recommend Stealth or a\n\tFace skill like Persuasion) puts you well ahead of nearly any other skill\n\tuser. Rogues are great at mitidating damage from attacks (Uncanny Dodge) and\n\tfrom area damage (Evasion), but mental saves are often a problem, so Vedalken\n\tDispassion is a nice defense."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-rogue-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Note that the rules which allow you to replace redundant skill/tool\n\tproficiencies only apply to backgrounds, so if you choose Thieves’ Tools with\n\tTireless Precision, you are giving up an additional proficiency in exchange\n\tfor that d4. It’s probably still a good idea."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-sorcerer",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Sorcerer",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-sorcerer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-sorcerer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "An extra skill will help you expand beyond Face skills, and Vedalken\n\tDispassion is a helpful defense since sorcerers have relatively poor mental\n\tsaves compared to other full casters."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-warlock",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Warlock",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-warlock",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-warlock-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "An extra skill will help you expand beyond Face skills, but their saving\n\tthrows are mostly already good since they’re proficienct in both Wisdom and\n\tCharisma saves, so Vedalken Dispassion isn’t hugely important."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-wizard",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Wizard",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-wizard",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-wizard-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Wizards don’t have much use for tools and have few good skill options. Their\n\tsaving throws are mostly already good since they’re proficienct in both\n\tIntelligence and Wisdom saves, so Vedalken Dispassion does little to address\n\tthe Wizard’s frailties."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Vedalken Classes (Default Rules)",
      "sourceAnchor": "classes-default",
      "blocks": []
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-artificer",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Artificer",
      "sourceAnchor": "artificer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-artificer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "An Intelligence increase is all that you really need to succeed as an\n\tartificer. Vedalken Dispassion will offer some additional protection against\n\tspells, so you’ll be very durable if you equip yourself well. Be sure to get\n\tproficiency in Perception to capitalize on the Vedalken’s Wisdom increase."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-barbarian",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Barbarian",
      "sourceAnchor": "barbarian",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-barbarian-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Bad ability spread."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-bard",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Bard",
      "sourceAnchor": "bard",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-bard-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The additional skill/tool proficiencies and Tireless Precision are the only\n\tthing which really caters to the Bard."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-cleric",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Cleric",
      "sourceAnchor": "cleric",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-cleric-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Wisdom increase and Vedalken Dispassion."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-druid",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Druid",
      "sourceAnchor": "druid",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-druid-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Wisdom increase and Vedalken Dispassion, which should still work in Wild\n\tShape since it’s a mental trait rather than a feature of your body. You won’t\n\tget to be a partially-amphibious wolf, sadly."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-fighter",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Fighter",
      "sourceAnchor": "fighter",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-fighter-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Bad ability spread."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-monk",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Monk",
      "sourceAnchor": "monk",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-monk-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Vedalken’s best option for a martial class, but it’s not a good\n\tchoice."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-paladin",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Paladin",
      "sourceAnchor": "paladin",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-paladin-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Bad ability spread."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-ranger",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Ranger",
      "sourceAnchor": "ranger",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-ranger-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Bad ability spread."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-rogue",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Rogue",
      "sourceAnchor": "rogue",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-rogue-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Bad ability spread, which is a shame because combining Expertise and Tireless\n\tPrecision seems like so much fun. Maybe worth 1-levle multiclass dip?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-sorcerer",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Sorcerer",
      "sourceAnchor": "sorcerer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-sorcerer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "No Charisma increase."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-warlock",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Warlock",
      "sourceAnchor": "warlock",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-warlock-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "No Charisma increase."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-wizard",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Wizard",
      "sourceAnchor": "wizard",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-wizard-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "An Intelligence increase, and Vedalken Dispassion will help protect you.\n\tYou’ll still be frail, but when some other spellcaster tries to mind control\n\tyou you’ll have some extra protection."
